[
  {
    "beat": 1,
    "flux": "A weathered lighthouse keeper, hooded and rain-damp, crouches over a dented copper bucket at a black-sand shore, cradling a translucent silver fish that emits a soft pulsing blue-white bioluminescence. Composition places her low in the left foreground, bucket near bottom center, lighthouse tower looming vertically behind; shallow depth of field from a 50mm prime lens, medium close-up. Dawn light is pale peach and cool steel blue, with wet gull-wing reflections. Palette: seafoam, slate, brass, luminous pearl. Style: painterly cinematic realism, delicate rim light, gritty coastal texture, high detail, no text.",
    "ltx": "Silent dawn shoreline. The keeper's gloved fingers gently lift the fish from brine; its light pulses in slow rhythmic throbs. Water drips, ripples, and tiny foam crests break around the bucket. Camera starts low and still, then slowly pushes in toward the fish with slight handheld micro-drift; no pans, no music, no speech, pacing quiet and meditative."
  },
  {
    "beat": 2,
    "flux": "Lighthouse keeper ascends a narrow spiral staircase, seen from a low interior angle looking up, one weathered hand pressing the rusted iron rail, the other holding a lantern-sized glass jar containing the glowing fish. The curved stair coils upward into shadow, with iron bars and a porthole cutting slants of storm light. Lens: 35mm, slightly wide, medium shot; shallow focus on fish and keeper's profile. Light: deep blue-grey exterior storm light mixed with warm amber jar glow and faint moonlit porthole. Palette: oxidized copper, navy, charcoal, gold. Style: moody cinematic realism, tactile wood, wet metal, dramatic chiaroscuro, high detail, no text.",
    "ltx": "Silent interior spiral stair. The keeper climbs steadily upward, boots striking iron steps; the jar bobs slightly with her gait and the fish's glow pulses faster as storm light flickers through the porthole. Rusted rail shakes subtly; rain streaks glass. Camera follows in a slow ascending crane-like move from behind and below, tilting upward with her; pacing tightens with increasing sway, no music, no speech."
  },
  {
    "beat": 3,
    "flux": "Inside a circular lighthouse lamp room, keeper releases the glowing fish into a shallow brass basin near the Fresnel lens. The fish radiates intense gold-ivory light, filling the glass panes, brass mechanisms, and curved rail with volumetric beams. Composition: centered symmetrical lamp room, keeper small in lower left, basin and lens dominate center, circular windows framing storm outside. Lens: 24mm wide, medium shot, deep focus. Light: radiant gold core, soft white highlights, cool blue storm rim. Palette: molten gold, cream, brass, midnight blue. Style: epic cinematic realism, luminous particles, intricate lens detail, dramatic scale, painterly glow, no text.",
    "ltx": "Silent lamp room transformation. The fish swims in slow circles in the brass basin, its glow swelling in pulses; gold light floods glass panels and brass edges, then the great lens ignites from white to warm gold. Dust motes and steam rise in the beams. Camera: slow 180-degree orbital move around the lamp room, gradually tightening on the lens, pacing building from stillness to radiant acceleration, no music, no speech."
  },
  {
    "beat": 4,
    "flux": "A battered wooden sailing ship on a black storm sea, viewed from a low ocean level, passes between jagged sea rocks illuminated by a horizontal shaft of golden lighthouse beam from the right. The beam cuts through rain and spray like solid light. Composition: ship in left third, rocks in midground, beam diagonally from upper right, lighthouse small at upper edge. Lens: 85mm telephoto compressed view, medium-long shot, shallow focus on rigging and wet decks. Light: deep blue-black night with saturated gold beam, white foam highlights. Palette: indigo, charcoal, burnished gold, foam white. Style: dramatic cinematic realism, weathered rigging detail, painterly storm atmosphere, high dynamic range, no text.",
    "ltx": "Silent sea rescue. The ship heaves and trims sail as it crosses the frame, rigging straining; waves roll, rain falls, spray breaks over rocks. The gold beam sweeps steadily across the water, guiding the bow between jagged reefs. Camera: slow dolly and arc from a low side angle, tracking with the ship and pulling back slightly as it clears the rocks; pacing tense but controlled, no music, no speech."
  }
]
